    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nOccupying an enviable position on one of Greystones' most established and sought-after residential roads, Hadley Rille is a substantial detached family home extending to approximately 201 sq.m (2,164 sq.ft), offering a rare opportunity to acquire a home of exceptional character and provenance in the very heart of this vibrant coastal town. Lovingly owned and occupied by the same family since it was purchased new in 1970, the property takes its name from the famous lunar feature explored during the Apollo 15 mission, reflecting the spirit and optimism of a remarkable era.\n\nSet behind off-street parking and enjoying a wonderfully sunny west-facing rear garden, the accommodation is both generous and versatile, with a layout ideally suited to modern family life. The ground floor comprises two spacious bedrooms, a bathroom, kitchen, large living room and a separate study, while upstairs offers two generous double bedrooms, including a principal bedroom with dressing room, together with a family bathroom, study / home office space and ample eaves storage accommodation.\n\nWhile the property has been meticulously maintained throughout the years, its conservative décor presents an exciting opportunity for the discerning purchaser to modernise and create a home tailored to their own taste and requirements. The generous proportions, flexible floorplan and exceptionally central maritime location combine to offer enormous potential in a setting where opportunities of this nature rarely arise.\n\nThe backdrop of Hadley Rille is truly exceptional. Situated just moments from Greystones' bustling Main Street, residents enjoy immediate access to an outstanding array of cafés, restaurants, boutiques, bakeries, supermarkets, saunas and everyday conveniences. The town's renowned marina, beaches, harbour and scenic coastal walks are all within easy strolling distance, providing an enviable maritime lifestyle that balances recreation and relaxation. Excellent transport links, including the DART, Dublin Bus and nearby N11/M50 corridor, ensure seamless connectivity to Dublin City Centre and beyond, while a selection of highly regarded schools and sporting amenities further enhance the appeal of this outstanding family location.\n\nHadley Rille represents a rare opportunity to secure a landmark family home in the very heart of Greystones, combining a rich history, exceptional potential and an unrivalled coastal village setting. Viewing is highly recommended and can be arranged by prior appointment though the MySherryFitz app or the Greystones office."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Porch - \nSliding glazed door and porch light.\n\nEntrance Hallway: - \nWide entrance with wooden plank flooring, access to understairs storage and alarm panel.\n\nSitting Room: - 7.01m x 6.82m\nExceptionally large reception with window to the front garden. Brick fireplace with wooden mantle. Wall and ceiling lights.\n\nBedroom 4 / Playroom: - 3.33m x 3.40m\nWooden plank flooring, window overlooking rear garden.\n\nKitchen / Dining Room: - 4.53m x 3.40m\nFitted floor and eye level units, stainless steel sink and drainer, door to west facing rear garden. Electric hob and oven, extractor fan, washing machine, fridge / freezer.\n\nBedroom 3: - 3.58m x 3.42m\nA bright double bedroom with sliding glazed doors to rear garden.\n\nShower Room: - 2.52m x 1.87m\nFrosted window, WC, pedestal wash hand basin, part tiled walls and tiled corner shower unit with glazed door.\n\nTV Room / Den: - 2.44m x 4.67m\nWooden floor. Sliding glazed doors to the front garden with frosted window to the side.\n\nUpstairs: - \nOff a bright gallery landing\n\nMain Bedroom 1: - 4.79m x 3.60m\nA bright double bedroom with build in wardrobe storage holding door to access extensive eaves storage area. Overlooking the rear garden with distant view of the Great Sugarloaf. Off which:\n\nDressing Room: - 2.17m x 3.40m\nPotential for use as a fifth bedroom space, a bright versatile space with eaves access.\n\nFamily Bathroom: - 2.69m x 2.69m\nFrosted window, WC, pedestal wash hand basin, bath with mixer tap.\n\nStudy/Storage - 2.17m x 4.13m\nVelux light, access to eaves storage\n\nBedroom 2: - 2.71m x 4.60m\nA large double positioned to the front of the house\n\nHotpress: - \nShelved for storage\n\nOutside: - \nGated off street parking, and hedging surrounding a lawn area to the front. Side passage brings one to the beautifully sunny west facing rear garden. A peaceful haven boasting mature planting and well-defined boundary walls, along with paved patio area offering the perfect spot to enjoy the afternoon and evening private suntrap. Garden shed, outdoor tap and block-built boiler house.\n\n"
      },
